  "id": "perceived-risk",
  "term": "perceived risk",
  "definition": "Perceived risk is a person’s sense of the possible costs or negative consequences of an action. In this study, it refers to how risky students believe it is to seek feedback, with higher self-efficacy linked to seeing less risk.",
